# =============================================================================
# BiNGS Bulk RNA-seq Course — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# The shared hands_on/ tree is ~12 GB (data + indices + container + fastqs).
# We push only the browseable stuff (code + small tables + figures + READMEs)
# and let a `bash engine/download_reference_data.sh` step pull the large blobs
# back into place on Minerva (symlinks to the shared reference).

# ─── Non-RNA data (out of scope for this repo) ───────────────────────────────
data_chip/
data_atac/

# ─── Big binary blobs — student clones symlink these back via download script
# Singularity container (7.1 GB)
engine/singularity_containers/*.sif

# Full STAR + Salmon indices (~2 GB + ~800 MB) — indices are pre-built, huge
engine/annotation/star/
engine/annotation/salmon/

# chr5 genome FASTA (177 MB) — kept alongside code as reference material via symlink
engine/annotation/data/GRCh38.p13.chr5.genome.fa

# Raw fastqs (200-300 MB each)
data_rna/reduced_chr5/raw/fastq/*.fastq
data_rna/reduced_chr5/raw/fastq/*.fastq.gz

# STAR alignment BAMs (60-65 MB each) — students regenerate in session 4
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/star/*.bam
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/star/*.bam.bai

# Salmon quant intermediates (medium size; students regenerate)
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/salmon/*/aux_info/
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/salmon/*/libParams/
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/salmon/*/logs/

# TrimGalore trimmed fastqs (large intermediates; students regenerate)
data_rna/reduced_chr5/preprocessed/trimgalore/*_trimmed.fq.gz

# ─── R session artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf
*.Rproj

# ─── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Scratch / logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*_lsf_stdout*
*_lsf_stderr*
